Subject: libdeflate: use the generic C code instead of the x86 branch

The clang for the PS5 defines __SCE__, so the AVX-VNNI/AVX-512 intrinsic headers are not
included, while libdeflate tries to call them. Disable its x86 branch (plain C instead).

---
diff --git a/third-party/libdeflate/common_defs.h b/third-party/libdeflate/common_defs.h
index 094d438..12f086d 100644
--- a/third-party/libdeflate/common_defs.h
+++ b/third-party/libdeflate/common_defs.h
@@ -77,7 +77,7 @@
 #    define ARCH_ARM32
 #  endif
 #else
-#  if defined(__x86_64__)
+#  if 0 /* PS5: __SCE__ clang omits AVX-VNNI/AVX-512 intrinsics; use generic C */
 #    define ARCH_X86_64
 #  elif defined(__i386__)
 #    define ARCH_X86_32
